\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Interim Community Development Director Michael Codron highlighted the Project Pulse study session scheduled for August 26, 2025, at 5:00 PM in the City Council Chambers. Project Pulse refers to the current public outreach efforts to ensure staff and City decision-makers have a clear understanding of community sentiment before major decisions are made regarding two public properties: Parking Lot 3 and 400 Manhattan Beach Boulevard.\line\line Waste Management (WM) Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced that collection services will be postponed by one day due to the Labor Day Holiday.\line\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson provided an update on the recent uptick in coyote sightings in the City, reporting 128 sightings within the past year. The Parking and Animal Control section has been actively engaged in coyote management to make the environment less hospitable. Flyers with information and guidance are available through the Police Department. Police Chief Johnson also responded to City Council questions.\line\line Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced upcoming events, including a Writing Dynamic College Essays Workshop on September 3, 2025, from 5:00 PM - 6:30 PM, and a Cello Performance by Chelsea Wong on August 30, 2025, from 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM. She also responded to City Council questions.\line\line Ray Joseph announced a protest regarding SB79 (high-density housing) near the Strand and Manhattan Beach Boulevard scheduled for August 23, 2025, at 9:00 AM.\line\line Culture Club South Bay Founder and Executive Director Allison Hales announced that the local non-profit provides free beach access to diverse youth of color twice a year at Bruce\rquote s Beach and is seeking volunteers aged 14 and older.\line\line Councilmember Howorth reminded the community that tomorrow is the first day of school for the Manhattan Beach Unified School District and wished everyone a safe, healthy, and successful school year.\line\line\pard Mayor Pro Tem Franklin announced that the Superior Court of Los Angeles County is recruiting alternate members for the grand jury.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


